# Kaggle pack export -- build_kaggle_pack.ps1 lands pack\ at the repo root
# by default: ~40 MB of Linux ELF binaries, regenerable in minutes with that
# script, so it must never enter git history (nor the Docker build context).
pack/

# Staging directory used by build-native.yml: `--output type=local` writes the
# pack-exporter image's ROOT filesystem here, so the pack arrives nested as
# pack-export/pack/... The workflow then normalises it to pack/. Kept separate
# from `pack/` on purpose -- collapsing the export into ./pack instead would
# produce pack/pack/bin/..., which is exactly the bug this name avoids.
pack-export/

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# CMake build tree for the C++ normalizer.
#
# This directory was committed by accident -- 22 files including CMakeCache.txt,
# .ninja_deps, .ninja_log, a compiler-id binary and normalizer.exe itself. That
# is not merely untidy: CMakeCache.txt records ABSOLUTE paths of the machine that
# generated it, so the moment CI checked it out, cmake refused to configure --
#
#   CMake Error: The current CMakeCache.txt directory
#   'D:/a/T_Dubber/T_Dubber/cpp_accelerator/build/CMakeCache.txt' is different
#   than the directory 'C:/Program Files/Git/mingw64/lib/Git/cmake-build/...'
#   where 'CMakeCache.txt' was created.
#
# The recorded path was a Git-Bash-mangled path from the original author's
# machine, so it could never match any CI runner. A build tree is regenerated in
# seconds by the CI job that needs it, so it has no business in history.
cpp_accelerator/build/

# Same reasoning for any other stray CMake tree.
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
.ninja_deps
.ninja_log
compile_commands.json

# Out-of-tree build directory used by .github/workflows/build-native.yml. The
# Windows job builds normalizer.exe here instead of inside cpp_accelerator/, so
# a CMakeCache.txt can never be committed into the source tree by accident.
.build/
